 "path": "continual_arc_notes.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC observed pattern\n\nIn task `task-1e877ea2`, each input had a uniform background and two large rectangular colored regions, with scattered pixels of other colors throughout the background and occasional intrusions inside the rectangles. The output preserved the two rectangles, filled each rectangle uniformly with its dominant color, and replaced every other cell (including stray/outlier pixels) with the background color. Demo example: background 3, rectangles 0 and 1; test: background 6, rectangles 8 and 5. For similar puzzles, identify the large solid rectangular objects and their dominant colors, then clean noise by rebuilding those rectangles and setting everything else to the background. This is an observed heuristic, not proof that future instances always share this rule.\n"
}
